From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: the KDA block writes its output again

The 0019 port replaced the forward's KDA body call and dropped the
`kda_block.fill` line beside it, so no KDA layer ever wrote its o_proj into
`out`: every prompt and decode step read stale rows and the replies came back
as token salad while every rank reported healthy. The source era calls
`if (out) |o| try kda_block.fill(f.set(), f.stream, k, s, 0, rows, o);` right
after bodyProfile; this restores it. Bisected by booting each arm and reading
its own reply: arms through 0017 answered the count prompt correctly, adding
0019 alone turned it to garbage, and with this line the full stack answers the
same text as the stock pin.

Gates: the full stack (0001..0037) answers the smoke prompt with the pin's own
text; the stream cells' digests equal the pin's at the same stream count.
diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_forward.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_forward.zig
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_forward.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_forward.zig
@@ -288,6 +288,7 @@
                 }
                 const conv = st.conv + li * 3 * st.conv_c * 2;
                 try kda_block.bodyProfile(f.set(), &f.m.kda, f.stream, k, s, b.normed, c.hidden, rows, conv, st.recAt(cur, li), !b.prefill and f.kda_wide, b.prefill, f.prof, if (b.prefill) kda_chunk.prompt(&f.m.chunked, st.pos) else null, if (f.l2pfFor()) |p| .{ .l2 = p, .layer = l.index } else null);
+                if (out) |o| try kda_block.fill(f.set(), f.stream, k, s, 0, rows, o);
                 if (b.prefill) st.cur[li] = 1 - cur; // a prompt chunk keeps every row: the layer commits now
             },
             .mla => |a| {
